schema stdio.deflate.op
start op

# P2-FG2: `protocol::OpBinary::encode_op`/`decode_op` (../🦀️component.rs) forward straight to
# `dsl::variants_binary::encode_op`/`decode_op` (🗣️dsl/🦀️component.rs `OpRt` region) -- this was
# ALREADY real binary before this wave touched it, NOT the F6-era `print_op().into_bytes()`
# text-as-binary shortcut (confirmed by direct reading, not assumed: `encode_op` calls
# `os_pack::encode_record_body`, never `print_op` -- matches the P2-W0 census's own "OpBinary via
# real binary" list, which names `deflate` explicitly). Upgrading an already-real codec is a
# no-op, not a mistake -- see `📖️grammar-recipe.md` §4's own deliverable checklist item.
#
# Layout, byte-for-byte, per that helper's own convention (`OP_BINARY_FORMAT`): a fixed `format`
# byte (always `1`), the matched `DeflateMutation` variant's ordinal as a `varint` (declaration
# order: `NoMutation`=0, `SetSnapshot`=1, `SetCompressionParams`=2, `SetPresetDictionary`=3,
# `SetPayload`=4 -- `dsl::DslVariants::variants()`'s own emission order), then the variant's own
# field payload via `os_pack::encode_record_body(spec, record)` -- itself a varint-prefixed
# STRING-SYMBOL TABLE followed by a generic, self-describing per-field-id TAG+value wire
# (`🎒️pack/🔢️value/🦀️component.rs`). This inner wire is the FRAMEWORK's own generic record-body
# encoding -- shared verbatim by every `#[derive(dsl::DslRecord)]`/`DslOps`/`DslDiff` type in the
# whole repo, not anything specific to `stdio.deflate` -- and is genuinely NOT expressible by
# this dialect's `Array`/`Ref`/`repeat` primitives as they stand today (no dynamic per-field TAG
# dispatch keyed by a runtime field-id, no symbol-table back-reference resolution). Filed under
# the ALREADY-consolidated `txt-opbinary-record-body-wire-is-framework-generic` gap
# (`📖️grammar-recipe.md` §5) -- txt hit this identical shape first; this wave's report cites it
# rather than re-filing it. Modeled honestly: `format`/`ordinal` are genuinely, individually
# byte-walked and validated; the remaining record-body bytes are one opaque tail.
framing record
field format u8
field ordinal varint
chain bytes
